member.summary:
Per-property limits probed from the actual camera at runtime, keyed by setting
            name (e.g. "brightness"). Used to size each slider to what the camera really accepts;
            absent entries fall back to the client's default ranges.

member.exception:
InvalidArgument for  or a level outside 0-100;
FailedPrecondition "USB relay module not connected" when no backlight output at
all is attached; Unavailable "LED board backlight command failed: <cause>"
or "USB relay module write failed: <cause>" when the output's command failed;
Unimplemented on a server without backlight support. A server from before the
LED-board backlights ignores the level.

member.summary:
The column's USB hub is mounted upside down (kiosk.camera_hub_upside_down): the
automatic camera order is mirrored. Off unless the working copy holds a real true;
a server from before the setting sends nothing here (off).
